Answer: On the circle below, you have  $A \equiv (x, y), \ B \equiv (0, 0), \ C \equiv (x, 0)$ : 

 You see the triangle  $ABC$  is a right triangle since  $\hat{ACB} = 90$ °. You have thus those relations:
 \begin{equation}
\sin \theta := \frac{|AC|}{|AB|}
\end{equation} 
 \begin{equation}
\cos \theta := \frac{|BC|}{|AB|}
\end{equation} 
 \begin{equation}
\tan \theta := \frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta} = \frac{|AC|}{|BC|} = \frac{y}{x}
\end{equation} 
Your angle  $\theta$  is thus:
 \begin{equation}
\theta = \arctan{\left( \frac{y}{x} \right)} \ (x \neq 0)
\end{equation} 
